    "turn_text": "I got to tell you, the only poll that matters is on election day. You know that, Sean. As I traveled around the country last week and I'm headed out to Iowa today to a couple of stops. Donald Trump and I were to get through in Detroit this morning. I mean, the Detroit Economic Club usually draws a couple of hundred people. There were several thousand people that came out for that speech today. The reception alone had more people that came out to say hello to us before the event than usually come to these gatherings altogether. So the rope lines that I'm seeing, even events that Karen and I are attending are extraordinary. I just have to believe the enthusiasm that we're seeing across these countries, of a connection that Donald Trump has made to Americans at every level. That speech today was an aspirational speech that simply said, look, if we will embrace new leadership, it will get back to what we know works, which is less taxes, less regulation, more American energy and smarter trade deals, that this country can come roaring back. I think people are responding to that message. They're responding to that clear-eyed leadership.",
